IO-10: store the number of barrels as an int

TConduit.barrels was a char and link_readXsectParams() stored the Barrels
item with (char)atoi(...). Counts above 127 wrapped: 300 barrels became 44,
and 200 became -56 (rejected as ERROR 114) where char is signed but stayed 200
where it is unsigned. Declare the field int and drop the cast. Every use of
the field is arithmetic or a %d format, so nothing else changes.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-10_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..4756fdb 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@ int link_readXsectParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
         {
             i = atoi(tok[6]);
             if ( i <= 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, tok[6]);
-            else Conduit[Link[j].subIndex].barrels = (char)i;
+            else Conduit[Link[j].subIndex].barrels = i;
         }
 
         // --- parse culvert code if present
diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/objects.h b/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
index 6b54d76..c9a6d56 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/objects.h
@@ -731,7 +731,7 @@ typedef struct
 {
    double        length;          // conduit length (ft)
    double        roughness;       // Manning's n
-   char          barrels;         // number of barrels
+   int           barrels;         // number of barrels
    //-----------------------------
    double        modLength;       // modified conduit length (ft)
    double        roughFactor;     // roughness factor for DW routing
